; ============================================================================
; PresApp.rgr — the presentation editor, as one class a browser holds.
; ============================================================================
;
;   ┌──────────────┬──────────────────────────────────────┐
;   │ ScriptEditor │  stage: the slide at the playhead    │
;   │  (markdown)  ├──────────────────────────────────────┤
;   │              │  tracks: text · speech · animation   │
;   │              ├──────────────────────────────────────┤
;   │              │  filmstrip                           │
;   └──────────────┴──────────────────────────────────────┘
;
; Everything on the canvas is EVG: the editor paints into the chrome list,
; the tracks and the filmstrip frames are an element tree laid out by
; `pres.css`, and each slide is a display list of its own (`stageJson`,
; `thumbJson`) that the host draws through a camera into the rectangle
; `layoutJson` names. The toolbar, the menus and the browser's own APIs are
; the host's HTML — this class never learns what a button looks like.
;
; TIME is the host's. It says what time it is (`setTime`) and reads back what
; time the app agreed to (`currentTime`): in a presentation the clock stops
; at the next build step until a click releases it, so the host's clock is
; rebased on the answer. Nothing here counts frames.
;
; What the host is asked to do leaves as strings through `takeRequest()`,
; so the class runs under Node in a check exactly as it does in a tab.
; ============================================================================

